IMPORT prelude

-- Corporations Act 2001 (Commonwealth of Australia) -- what Daniel's company Jarrah Legal Technologies Pty Ltd meets in the Act,
-- from registration to sale: registering a proprietary company and who may and must be its directors (ss 9AC, 113, 114, 117,
-- 201A, 201B, 1272B, 1272C); directors' duties (ss 180 to 184) and the duty to disclose a material personal interest (s 191);
-- offers of shares that need no disclosure document (s 708(1), (5), (8), (9), (11)) and the proprietary company's bar on
-- fundraising that would need one (s 113(3)); preference shares (s 254A(2)); dividends (s 254T); share buy-backs (ss 257A, 257B,
-- 257C, 257D, 257E, with s 250MA for a special resolution); subsidiaries and related bodies corporate (ss 46, 50); the takeovers
-- prohibition (s 606(1)); continuous disclosure (ss 674(2), 674A(3), (4), 676); and insider trading (ss 1042A, 1042C, 1042D,
-- 1043A, 1043D).
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 149, compilation date 19 September 2026, includes amendments to Act No. 87, 2026 (register id
-- C2026C00432), as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A00818.txt (retrieved 13 October 2026). The compilation is in
-- 7 volumes; the deposit joins them.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0011 (subjects/au/requirements.jsonl), priority 1, raised 7 times by the Western Australian
-- cradle-to-grave life of Daniel (workbench scenarios au/wa/cradle-to-grave-daniel): d043 (15 March 2031, Jarrah registered, 70%
-- Daniel, 10% Priya, 20% a sophisticated investor for $500,000: what registration needs, who is a director and what he owes, is
-- the placement exempt from disclosure?); d050 (1 September 2035, Series A, $5,000,000 for 25% from a fund that is a
-- sophisticated investor: is the issue exempt?); d064 (31 March 2042, a selective buy-back of the investor's shares, the
-- shareholder approval, the solvency test); d065 (15 June 2043, Jarrah acquires Formly: subsidiary and related bodies
-- corporate); d071 (30 June 2050, Jarrah sold to a listed buyer for $40,000,000: is it a takeover?); d073 (1 September 2051,
-- non-executive director of a listed company: what may a director who knows something not do with the shares?); d081 (20 March
-- 2056, angel investments in five start-ups as a sophisticated investor: what is he not protected from?). SCOPED to those
-- questions and the definitions, conditions and exceptions needed to answer them. The chloe and jake lives do not cite the Act.
--
-- Not encoded: everything else in a seven-volume Act. In particular: the other subsections of s 708 (12) to (21) and s 708AA;
-- what a prospectus must contain; s 727 offences and civil liability for defective disclosure; the s 611 exceptions to the
-- takeovers prohibition (an input), relevant interest and voting power (ss 608 to 610, taken as given percentages); the
-- minimum holding, employee share and on-market buy-back definitions beyond their names; ss 257F to 257H beyond the 257B
-- table; insolvent trading (s 588G); the listing rules themselves (an input -- the Act's continuous disclosure duty applies only
-- where the listing rules require notification); company trading windows and trading policies (not in the Act); s 192
-- standing notices beyond their effect; penalties. Amounts the Act leaves to regulations (the net assets and gross income
-- figures in s 708(8)(c)) are INPUTS, never hard-coded.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text, following the conventions of the finished naive encodings (the
-- writing-l4-rules skill was not available in this session). No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no
-- human gate. NOT for public use. See NOTES.md.

§ `Corporations Act 2001 -- Jarrah`

§§ `9AC, 201B, 1272B, 1272C -- who is a director, who may be one, and the director identification number`

-- s 9AC(1): a director is "(a) a person who: (i) is appointed to the position of a director; or (ii) is appointed to the position
-- of an alternate director and is acting in that capacity; regardless of the name that is given to their position; and (b)
-- unless the contrary intention appears, a person who is not validly appointed as a director if: (i) they act in the position of
-- a director; or (ii) the directors of the company or body are accustomed to act in accordance with the person's instructions or
-- wishes (excluding advice given by the person in the proper performance of functions attaching to the person's professional
-- capacity or their business relationship with the directors or the corporation)."
-- s 201B(1): "Only an individual who is at least 18 may be appointed as a director of a company." (2): a person disqualified under
-- Part 2D.6 only with ASIC's permission (s 206GAB) or the Court's leave (s 206G).
-- s 1272B(1)(a): an ELIGIBLE OFFICER is a director who "(i) is appointed to the position of a director; or (ii) is appointed to
-- the position of an alternate director and is acting in that capacity" (or an officer of a prescribed kind; the Registrar may
-- exclude persons -- neither encoded). A de facto or shadow director under s 9AC(1)(b) is NOT within it.
-- s 1272C(1): "An eligible officer must have a director identification number." (2): not if the officer applied before the day
-- they first became an eligible officer (or within a period the regulations or the Registrar allow) and the application has not
-- been finally determined; (3): not if the officer "became an eligible officer without the officer's knowledge".
DECLARE Person HAS
    `age` IS A NUMBER
    `is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
    `appointed as a director` IS A BOOLEAN
    `appointed as an alternate director and acting as one` IS A BOOLEAN
    `acts in the position of a director` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the directors are accustomed to act on their instructions` IS A BOOLEAN
    `those instructions are only advice in a professional capacity or business relationship` IS A BOOLEAN
    `disqualified from managing corporations` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has ASIC permission or Court leave to be appointed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `ordinarily resides in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has a director identification number` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has a timely director identification number application still pending` IS A BOOLEAN
    `became an eligible officer without knowing` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is a director` IF
        `the person`'s `appointed as a director`
    OR  `the person`'s `appointed as an alternate director and acting as one`
    OR  `the person`'s `acts in the position of a director`
    OR  (    `the person`'s `the directors are accustomed to act on their instructions`
         AND (NOT `the person`'s `those instructions are only advice in a professional capacity or business relationship`))

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person may be appointed a director` IF
        `the person`'s `is an individual`
    AND `the person`'s `age` AT LEAST 18
    AND (    (NOT `the person`'s `disqualified from managing corporations`)
         OR  `the person`'s `has ASIC permission or Court leave to be appointed`)

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is an eligible officer` IF
        `the person`'s `appointed as a director`
    OR  `the person`'s `appointed as an alternate director and acting as one`

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person contravenes s 1272C` IF
        `the person is an eligible officer` `the person`
    AND (NOT `the person`'s `has a director identification number`)
    AND (NOT `the person`'s `has a timely director identification number application still pending`)
    AND (NOT `the person`'s `became an eligible officer without knowing`)

§§ `113(1), 114, 117, 201A -- registering a proprietary company`

-- s 117(1): "To register a company, a person must lodge an application with ASIC." (2) it must state, among other things: (a) the
-- type of company; (b) the proposed name (unless the ACN is to be used); (c) the name and address of each person who consents to
-- become a member; (d), (f) the names, date and place of birth and address of each person who consents in writing to become a
-- director; (g) the registered office; (k) for a company limited by shares, the number and class of shares each member agrees in
-- writing to take up and the amount each agrees to pay; (ma) whether there will be an ultimate holding company; (n) the State or
-- Territory. (4): "The application must be in the prescribed form." (5): "An applicant must have the consents and agreements
-- referred to in subsection (2) when the application is lodged." Items (e), (h), (j), (l), (m), (mb) apply only in cases Jarrah
-- is not (a secretary, a public company, a separate place of business, a guarantee company, a holding company) and are not
-- encoded. s 118(1): if an application is lodged, ASIC "MAY" register the company -- the Act states no duty to register.
-- s 113(1): "A company must have no more than 50 non-employee shareholders if it is to ... be registered as a proprietary
-- company". s 114: "A company needs to have at least 1 member." s 201A(1): "A proprietary company must have at least 1 director.
-- That director must ordinarily reside in Australia." (The CSF rules in s 113(2)(c), (d) and s 201A(1A) are not encoded.)
DECLARE Application HAS
    `states the type of company` IS A BOOLEAN
    `states the proposed name or uses the ACN` IS A BOOLEAN
    `states each member's name and address` IS A BOOLEAN
    `states each director's names, date and place of birth and address` IS A BOOLEAN
    `states the registered office` IS A BOOLEAN
    `states the shares each member agrees to take up and pay for` IS A BOOLEAN
    `states whether there will be an ultimate holding company` IS A BOOLEAN
    `states the State or Territory` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is in the prescribed form` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the applicant holds the written consents and agreements` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the application` IS AN Application
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the application meets s 117` IF
        `the application`'s `states the type of company`
    AND `the application`'s `states the proposed name or uses the ACN`
    AND `the application`'s `states each member's name and address`
    AND `the application`'s `states each director's names, date and place of birth and address`
    AND `the application`'s `states the registered office`
    AND `the application`'s `states the shares each member agrees to take up and pay for`
    AND `the application`'s `states whether there will be an ultimate holding company`
    AND `the application`'s `states the State or Territory`
    AND `the application`'s `is in the prescribed form`
    AND `the application`'s `the applicant holds the written consents and agreements`

GIVEN `non-employee shareholders` IS A NUMBER, `members` IS A NUMBER, `directors` IS A NUMBER, `directors resident in Australia` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proprietary company meets the numbers` IF
        `non-employee shareholders` AT MOST 50
    AND `members` AT LEAST 1
    AND `directors` AT LEAST 1
    AND `directors resident in Australia` AT LEAST 1

§§ `180 to 184 -- directors' duties`

-- s 180(1): a director or other officer "must exercise their powers and discharge their duties with the degree of care and
-- diligence that a reasonable person would exercise" in their position. (2) the BUSINESS JUDGMENT RULE: one "who makes a business
-- judgment is taken to meet the requirements of subsection (1) ... if they: (a) make the judgment in good faith for a proper
-- purpose; and (b) do not have a material personal interest in the subject matter of the judgment; and (c) inform themselves ...
-- to the extent they reasonably believe to be appropriate; and (d) rationally believe that the judgment is in the best interests
-- of the corporation." It protects only s 180 and its common law and equitable equivalents.
-- s 181(1): "in good faith in the best interests of the corporation; and (b) for a proper purpose."
-- s 182(1): director, secretary, other officer or EMPLOYEE "must not improperly use their position" to gain an advantage or cause
-- detriment. s 183(1): a person who obtains information "because they are, or have been," a director, officer or employee must
-- not improperly use it; Note 1: "This duty continues after the person stops being an officer or employee".
-- s 184(1): an OFFENCE if the director "(a) are reckless; or (b) are dishonest; and fail to exercise their powers and discharge
-- their duties: (c) in good faith in the best interests of the corporation; or (d) for a proper purpose."
GIVEN `in good faith for a proper purpose` IS A BOOLEAN, `has a material personal interest in it` IS A BOOLEAN, `informed themselves as they reasonably believed appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN, `rationally believes it is in the company's best interests` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the business judgment rule protects the judgment` IF
        `in good faith for a proper purpose`
    AND (NOT `has a material personal interest in it`)
    AND `informed themselves as they reasonably believed appropriate`
    AND `rationally believes it is in the company's best interests`

GIVEN `acted in good faith in the company's best interests` IS A BOOLEAN, `acted for a proper purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 181(1) is contravened` IF
        (NOT `acted in good faith in the company's best interests`)
    OR  (NOT `acted for a proper purpose`)

GIVEN `acted in good faith in the company's best interests` IS A BOOLEAN, `acted for a proper purpose` IS A BOOLEAN, `was reckless` IS A BOOLEAN, `was dishonest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the s 184(1) offence is committed` IF
        (`was reckless` OR `was dishonest`)
    AND `s 181(1) is contravened` `acted in good faith in the company's best interests` `acted for a proper purpose`

GIVEN `obtained the information because they are or have been a director, officer or employee` IS A BOOLEAN, `improperly used it for an advantage or to cause detriment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 183(1) is contravened` IF
        `obtained the information because they are or have been a director, officer or employee`
    AND `improperly used it for an advantage or to cause detriment`

§§ `191 -- disclosing a material personal interest`

-- s 191(1): "A director of a company who has a material personal interest in a matter that relates to the affairs of the company
-- must give the other directors notice of the interest unless subsection (2) says otherwise." (2): no notice needed if (a) the
-- interest is one of eight kinds listed (held in common with the other members as a member; remuneration as a director; a
-- contract subject to members' approval; a guarantee or indemnity for a loan to the company; subrogation; directors' insurance;
-- a permitted indemnity; a contract with a related body corporate of which the director is a director); (b) "the company is a
-- proprietary company and the other directors are aware of the nature and extent of the interest"; (c) notice was already given
-- and the interest "has not materially increased"; (d) a standing notice under s 192 is still effective. (3): notice at a
-- directors' meeting "as soon as practicable", recorded in the minutes. (4): a contravention does not affect validity.
-- (5): "This section does not apply to a proprietary company that has only 1 director."
DECLARE Interest HAS
    `the director has a material personal interest relating to the company's affairs` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the company is a proprietary company` IS A BOOLEAN
    `number of directors` IS A NUMBER
    `the interest is of a kind listed in s 191(2)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the other directors are aware of its nature and extent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `notice already given and the interest has not materially increased` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a standing notice under s 192 is effective` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the interest` IS AN Interest
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the director must give notice under s 191` IF
        `the interest`'s `the director has a material personal interest relating to the company's affairs`
    AND (NOT (`the interest`'s `the company is a proprietary company` AND `the interest`'s `number of directors` EQUALS 1))
    AND (NOT `the interest`'s `the interest is of a kind listed in s 191(2)(a)`)
    AND (NOT (`the interest`'s `the company is a proprietary company` AND `the interest`'s `the other directors are aware of its nature and extent`))
    AND (NOT `the interest`'s `notice already given and the interest has not materially increased`)
    AND (NOT `the interest`'s `a standing notice under s 192 is effective`)

§§ `708, 113(3) -- offers of shares that need no disclosure document`

-- s 708(1): "Personal offers of a body's securities by a person do not need disclosure to investors under this Part if: (a) none
-- of the offers results in a breach of the 20 investors ceiling ...; and (b) none of the offers results in a breach of the $2
-- million ceiling". (2) a personal offer "may only be accepted by the person to whom it is made" and is made to someone likely to
-- be interested because of previous contact, a connection, or their statements. (3) an issue breaches the ceilings "if it results
-- in the number of people to whom securities of the body have been issued EXCEEDING 20 in any 12 month period" or "the amount
-- raised ... EXCEEDING $2 million in any 12 month period". (5) in counting, "disregard issues and sales that result from offers
-- that: (a) do not need a disclosure document because of any other subsection of this section; or (b) are not received in
-- Australia; or (c) are made under a disclosure document."
-- s 708(8) SOPHISTICATED INVESTORS: no disclosure if "(a) the minimum amount payable for the securities on acceptance ... is at
-- least $500,000; or (b) the amount payable ... and the amounts previously paid by the person for the body's securities of the
-- same class that are held by the person add up to at least $500,000; or (c) it appears from a certificate given by a qualified
-- accountant no more than 6 months before the offer is made that the person ... (i) has net assets of at least the amount
-- specified in regulations ...; or (ii) has a gross income for each of the last 2 financial years of at least the amount
-- specified in regulations ...; or (d) the offer is made to a company or trust controlled by a person who meets" (c)(i) or (ii).
-- (The certificate fields below may be the controller's, for (d).) The regulation amounts are INPUTS: the Act does not state them.
-- (9): "disregard any amount payable, or paid, to the extent to which it is to be paid, or was paid, out of money lent by the
-- person offering the securities or an associate."
-- s 708(11) PROFESSIONAL INVESTORS: no disclosure if made to "(a) a person covered by the definition of professional investor in
-- section 9 (except a person mentioned in paragraph (e) of the definition); or (b) a person who has or controls gross assets of at
-- least $10 million".
-- s 113(3): "A proprietary company must not engage in any activity that would require disclosure to investors under Chapter 6D,
-- except for: (a) an offer of its shares ... to: (i) existing shareholders of the company; or (ii) employees of the company or of
-- a subsidiary". (4): the transaction is not invalid; ASIC may require it to become a public company (s 165).
DECLARE Offer HAS
    `is a personal offer` IS A BOOLEAN
    `investors counted for s 708(1) in the 12 months, this offer included` IS A NUMBER
    `amount counted for s 708(1) in the 12 months, this offer included` IS A NUMBER
    `minimum amount payable on acceptance` IS A NUMBER
    `amount previously paid for same-class securities still held` IS A NUMBER
    `part paid out of money lent by the offeror or an associate` IS A NUMBER
    `has a qualified accountant's certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
    `whole months from the certificate to the offer` IS A NUMBER
    `further days from the certificate to the offer` IS A NUMBER
    `certified net assets` IS A NUMBER
    `certified gross income in each of the last 2 financial years` IS A NUMBER
    `is a professional investor otherwise than by paragraph (e)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `gross assets the offeree has or controls` IS A NUMBER
    `is made to an existing shareholder or an employee` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is received in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is made under a disclosure document` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the offer` IS AN Offer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 708(1) small scale applies` IF
        `the offer`'s `is a personal offer`
    AND `the offer`'s `investors counted for s 708(1) in the 12 months, this offer included` AT MOST 20
    AND `the offer`'s `amount counted for s 708(1) in the 12 months, this offer included` AT MOST 2000000

GIVEN `the offer` IS AN Offer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the certificate is no more than 6 months old` IF
        `the offer`'s `has a qualified accountant's certificate`
    AND (    `the offer`'s `whole months from the certificate to the offer` LESS THAN 6
         OR  (`the offer`'s `whole months from the certificate to the offer` EQUALS 6 AND `the offer`'s `further days from the certificate to the offer` EQUALS 0))

GIVEN `the offer` IS AN Offer
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount counted for s 708(8)(a)` MEANS
    `the offer`'s `minimum amount payable on acceptance` MINUS `the offer`'s `part paid out of money lent by the offeror or an associate`

GIVEN `the offer` IS AN Offer
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount counted for s 708(8)(b)` MEANS
    `the amount counted for s 708(8)(a)` `the offer` PLUS `the offer`'s `amount previously paid for same-class securities still held`

GIVEN `the offer` IS AN Offer, `the regulation net assets amount` IS A NUMBER, `the regulation gross income amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 708(8) sophisticated investor applies` IF
        `the amount counted for s 708(8)(a)` `the offer` AT LEAST 500000
    OR  `the amount counted for s 708(8)(b)` `the offer` AT LEAST 500000
    OR  (    `the certificate is no more than 6 months old` `the offer`
         AND (    `the offer`'s `certified net assets` AT LEAST `the regulation net assets amount`
              OR  `the offer`'s `certified gross income in each of the last 2 financial years` AT LEAST `the regulation gross income amount`))

GIVEN `the offer` IS AN Offer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 708(11) professional investor applies` IF
        `the offer`'s `is a professional investor otherwise than by paragraph (e)`
    OR  `the offer`'s `gross assets the offeree has or controls` AT LEAST 10000000

GIVEN `the offer` IS AN Offer, `the regulation net assets amount` IS A NUMBER, `the regulation gross income amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the offer needs no disclosure document` IF
        `s 708(1) small scale applies` `the offer`
    OR  `s 708(8) sophisticated investor applies` `the offer` `the regulation net assets amount` `the regulation gross income amount`
    OR  `s 708(11) professional investor applies` `the offer`

GIVEN `the offer` IS AN Offer, `the regulation net assets amount` IS A NUMBER, `the regulation gross income amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the issue is left out of the s 708(1) count` IF
        `s 708(8) sophisticated investor applies` `the offer` `the regulation net assets amount` `the regulation gross income amount`
    OR  `s 708(11) professional investor applies` `the offer`
    OR  (NOT `the offer`'s `is received in Australia`)
    OR  `the offer`'s `is made under a disclosure document`

GIVEN `the offer` IS AN Offer, `the regulation net assets amount` IS A NUMBER, `the regulation gross income amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proprietary company contravenes s 113(3)` IF
        (NOT `the offer needs no disclosure document` `the offer` `the regulation net assets amount` `the regulation gross income amount`)
    AND (NOT `the offer`'s `is made to an existing shareholder or an employee`)

§§ `254A(2), 254T -- preference shares and dividends`

-- s 254A(2): "A company can issue preference shares only if the rights attached to the preference shares with respect to" capital,
-- surplus assets and profits, dividends, voting and priority "are set out in the company's constitution (if any) or have been
-- otherwise approved by special resolution of the company".
-- s 254T(1): "A company must not pay a dividend unless: (a) the company's assets exceed its liabilities immediately before the
-- dividend is declared and the excess is sufficient for the payment of the dividend; and (b) the payment of the dividend is fair
-- and reasonable to the company's shareholders as a whole; and (c) the payment of the dividend does not materially prejudice the
-- company's ability to pay its creditors." (2): assets and liabilities per the accounting standards.
-- s 254T is about DIVIDENDS. A buy-back has its own test in s 257A(a) (below).
GIVEN `the rights are set out in the constitution` IS A BOOLEAN, `the rights were approved by special resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the company can issue the preference shares` IF
    `the rights are set out in the constitution` OR `the rights were approved by special resolution`

GIVEN `assets` IS A NUMBER, `liabilities` IS A NUMBER, `the dividend` IS A NUMBER, `fair and reasonable to the shareholders as a whole` IS A BOOLEAN, `materially prejudices paying creditors` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the company may pay the dividend` IF
        `assets` GREATER THAN `liabilities`
    AND `assets` MINUS `liabilities` AT LEAST `the dividend`
    AND `fair and reasonable to the shareholders as a whole`
    AND (NOT `materially prejudices paying creditors`)

§§ `257A to 257E, 250MA -- share buy-backs`

-- s 257A: "A company may buy back its own shares if: (a) the buy-back does not materially prejudice the company's ability to pay
-- its creditors; and (b) the company follows the procedures laid down in this Division."
-- s 257B(1) table (columns: minimum holding; employee share within / over the 10/12 limit; on-market within / over; equal access
-- scheme within / over; selective): ORDINARY RESOLUTION [257C] only for employee share, on-market and equal access buy-backs OVER
-- the 10/12 limit; SPECIAL OR UNANIMOUS RESOLUTION [257D] only for a SELECTIVE buy-back; LODGE OFFER DOCUMENTS [257E] for equal
-- access (both) and selective; 14 DAYS NOTICE [257F] for all but a minimum holding buy-back; cancel shares and notify ASIC for all.
-- (4): "The 10/12 limit ... is 10% of the smallest number, at any time during the last 12 months, of votes attaching to voting
-- shares". (5): exceeded if the votes bought back in the last 12 months plus those to be bought back "would exceed" it.
-- s 9: "selective buy-back means a buy-back that is none of" an equal access scheme, minimum holding, on-market or employee share
-- buy-back -- so there is no 10/12 limit column for it.
-- s 257D(1): the terms must be approved before the agreement by "(a) a special resolution passed at a general meeting of the
-- company, with no votes being cast in favour of the resolution by any person whose shares are proposed to be bought back or by
-- their associates; or (b) a resolution agreed to, at a general meeting, by all ordinary shareholders" (or be conditional on it).
-- s 250MA(b): a special resolution "must be passed by at least 75% of the votes cast by members who are entitled to vote".
-- (The seller's votes AGAINST are not barred and count among the votes cast.)
DECLARE BuyBack IS ONE OF
    `minimum holding buy-back`
    `employee share buy-back`
    `on-market buy-back`
    `equal access scheme buy-back`
    `selective buy-back`

GIVEN `smallest votes in the last 12 months` IS A NUMBER, `votes bought back in the last 12 months` IS A NUMBER, `votes to be bought back` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the buy-back exceeds the 10/12 limit` IF
    (`votes bought back in the last 12 months` PLUS `votes to be bought back`) TIMES 10 GREATER THAN `smallest votes in the last 12 months`

GIVEN `the kind` IS A BuyBack, `over the 10/12 limit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 257C ordinary resolution is needed` IF
    CONSIDER `the kind`
    WHEN `employee share buy-back` THEN `over the 10/12 limit`
    WHEN `on-market buy-back` THEN `over the 10/12 limit`
    WHEN `equal access scheme buy-back` THEN `over the 10/12 limit`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the kind` IS A BuyBack
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 257D special or unanimous resolution is needed` IF
    CONSIDER `the kind`
    WHEN `selective buy-back` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the kind` IS A BuyBack
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 257E offer documents must be lodged` IF
    CONSIDER `the kind`
    WHEN `equal access scheme buy-back` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `selective buy-back` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the kind` IS A BuyBack
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 257F 14 days notice is needed` IF
    CONSIDER `the kind`
    WHEN `minimum holding buy-back` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `votes for by others` IS A NUMBER, `votes for by the sellers or their associates` IS A NUMBER, `votes against` IS A NUMBER, `all ordinary shareholders agreed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the selective buy-back is approved under s 257D(1)` IF
        `all ordinary shareholders agreed`
    OR  (    `votes for by the sellers or their associates` EQUALS 0
         AND `votes for by others` TIMES 100 AT LEAST (`votes for by others` PLUS `votes against`) TIMES 75)

GIVEN `materially prejudices paying creditors` IS A BOOLEAN, `followed the Division's procedures` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the company may buy back its shares` IF
    (NOT `materially prejudices paying creditors`) AND `followed the Division's procedures`

§§ `46, 50 -- subsidiaries and related bodies corporate`

-- s 46: a body corporate is a subsidiary of another "if, and only if: (a) the other body: (i) controls the composition of the first
-- body's board; or (ii) is in a position to cast, or control the casting of, MORE THAN ONE-HALF of the maximum number of votes ...
-- at a general meeting of the first body; or (iii) holds more than one-half of the issued share capital of the first body
-- (excluding any part ... that carries no right to participate beyond a specified amount in a distribution ...); or (b) the first
-- body is a subsidiary of a subsidiary of the other body." (ss 47, 48 on board control and what to disregard are not encoded.)
-- s 50: where a body corporate is "(a) a holding company of another body corporate; or (b) a subsidiary of another body corporate;
-- or (c) a subsidiary of a holding company of another body corporate; the first-mentioned body and the other body are related to
-- each other."
GIVEN `controls the board` IS A BOOLEAN, `percent of the votes it can cast or control` IS A NUMBER, `percent of the participating issued share capital held` IS A NUMBER, `is a subsidiary of its subsidiary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the first body is a subsidiary` IF
        `controls the board`
    OR  `percent of the votes it can cast or control` GREATER THAN 50
    OR  `percent of the participating issued share capital held` GREATER THAN 50
    OR  `is a subsidiary of its subsidiary`

GIVEN `one is the holding company of the other` IS A BOOLEAN, `one is a subsidiary of the other` IS A BOOLEAN, `one is a subsidiary of the other's holding company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the bodies are related bodies corporate` IF
    `one is the holding company of the other` OR `one is a subsidiary of the other` OR `one is a subsidiary of the other's holding company`

§§ `606(1) -- the takeovers prohibition`

-- s 606(1): "A person must not acquire a relevant interest in issued voting shares in a company if: (a) the company is: (i) a
-- listed company; or (ii) an unlisted company with more than 50 members; and (b) the person acquiring the interest does so through
-- a transaction in relation to securities entered into by or on behalf of the person; and (c) because of the transaction, that
-- person's or someone else's voting power in the company increases: (i) from 20% or below to more than 20%; or (ii) from a starting
-- point that is above 20% and below 90%." (1A): not if a s 611 exception applies (an INPUT here). (3): count joint holders of a
-- parcel as 1 person. Note 3: an acquisition in a small unlisted company can still be caught "because of its effect on" another
-- company that is listed or has more than 50 members (not encoded).
GIVEN `the target is listed` IS A BOOLEAN, `members of the target` IS A NUMBER, `through a transaction by or for the acquirer` IS A BOOLEAN, `voting power before` IS A NUMBER, `voting power after` IS A NUMBER, `a s 611 exception applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 606(1) prohibits the acquisition` IF
        (`the target is listed` OR `members of the target` GREATER THAN 50)
    AND `through a transaction by or for the acquirer`
    AND `voting power after` GREATER THAN `voting power before`
    AND (    (`voting power before` AT MOST 20 AND `voting power after` GREATER THAN 20)
         OR  (`voting power before` GREATER THAN 20 AND `voting power before` LESS THAN 90))
    AND (NOT `a s 611 exception applies`)

§§ `674(2), 674A(3), (4), 676 -- continuous disclosure`

-- s 676(2): information is GENERALLY AVAILABLE if "(a) it consists of readily observable matter; or (b) ... (i) it has been made
-- known in a manner that would, or would be likely to, bring it to the attention of persons who commonly invest in securities of
-- a kind whose price or value might be affected by the information; and (ii) since it was so made known, a reasonable period for
-- it to be disseminated among such persons has elapsed." (3): also deductions, conclusions or inferences from either.
-- s 1042C(1) says the same for insider trading, in terms of "Division 3 financial products"; one rule serves both here.
-- s 674(2): if the listing rules require the entity to notify, "(b) the entity has information that those provisions require the
-- entity to notify ...; and (c) the information is not generally available; and (d) a reasonable person would expect the
-- information, if it were generally available, to have a material effect on the price or value of ED securities of the entity;
-- the ENTITY must notify the market operator". The duty is the listed entity's, not the director's.
-- s 674A(3): "A person who is involved in a listed disclosing entity's contravention of subsection (2) contravenes this
-- subsection." (4): not if the person proves they "(a) took all steps (if any) that were reasonable in the circumstances to ensure
-- that the listed disclosing entity complied ...; and (b) after doing so, believed on reasonable grounds that the listed disclosing
-- entity was complying".
GIVEN `readily observable` IS A BOOLEAN, `made known to those who commonly invest` IS A BOOLEAN, `a reasonable period to disseminate it has elapsed` IS A BOOLEAN, `deduced from such information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the information is generally available` IF
        `readily observable`
    OR  (`made known to those who commonly invest` AND `a reasonable period to disseminate it has elapsed`)
    OR  `deduced from such information`

GIVEN `the listing rules require notification of it` IS A BOOLEAN, `generally available` IS A BOOLEAN, `a reasonable person would expect a material effect on price` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the listed entity must notify the market operator` IF
        `the listing rules require notification of it`
    AND (NOT `generally available`)
    AND `a reasonable person would expect a material effect on price`

GIVEN `the entity contravened s 674A(2)` IS A BOOLEAN, `was involved in the contravention` IS A BOOLEAN, `took all reasonable steps to ensure compliance` IS A BOOLEAN, `then believed on reasonable grounds it was complying` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person contravenes s 674A(3)` IF
        `the entity contravened s 674A(2)`
    AND `was involved in the contravention`
    AND (NOT (`took all reasonable steps to ensure compliance` AND `then believed on reasonable grounds it was complying`))

§§ `1042A, 1042D, 1043A, 1043D -- insider trading`

-- s 1042A(1): "inside information means information in relation to which the following paragraphs are satisfied: (a) the
-- information is not generally available; (b) if the information were generally available--a reasonable person would expect it
-- to have a material effect on the price or value of particular Division 3 financial products." s 1042D: that is so "if (and only
-- if) the information would, or would be likely to, influence persons who commonly acquire Division 3 financial products in
-- deciding whether or not to acquire or dispose of" them.
-- s 1043A(1): if "(a) a person (the insider) possesses inside information; and (b) the insider knows, or ought reasonably to know,
-- that" (a) and (b) of the definition are satisfied, "the insider must not ... (c) apply for, acquire, or dispose of, relevant
-- Division 3 financial products ...; or (d) procure another person to" do so. (2): nor communicate it to another person who the
-- insider knows or ought reasonably to know would be likely to deal or procure, where the products "are able to be traded on a
-- financial market operated in this jurisdiction". "A person" -- not only a director or officer. The Act says nothing of company
-- trading windows; no window makes dealing on inside information lawful.
-- s 1043D: (1) "does not apply in respect of the acquisition of financial products pursuant to a requirement imposed by this Act".
-- (Underwriters, s 1043C; Chinese walls, s 1043F; and the other exceptions are not encoded.)
GIVEN `generally available` IS A BOOLEAN, `would influence those who commonly acquire such products` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the information is inside information` IF
    (NOT `generally available`) AND `would influence those who commonly acquire such products`

GIVEN `possesses the information` IS A BOOLEAN, `generally available` IS A BOOLEAN, `would influence those who commonly acquire such products` IS A BOOLEAN, `knows or ought reasonably to know both` IS A BOOLEAN, `the acquisition is required by this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 1043A(1) forbids dealing or procuring` IF
        `possesses the information`
    AND `the information is inside information` `generally available` `would influence those who commonly acquire such products`
    AND `knows or ought reasonably to know both`
    AND (NOT `the acquisition is required by this Act`)

GIVEN `possesses the information` IS A BOOLEAN, `generally available` IS A BOOLEAN, `would influence those who commonly acquire such products` IS A BOOLEAN, `knows or ought reasonably to know both` IS A BOOLEAN, `tradeable on a financial market in this jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN, `knows or ought to know the recipient would likely deal or procure` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 1043A(2) forbids communicating it` IF
        `possesses the information`
    AND `the information is inside information` `generally available` `would influence those who commonly acquire such products`
    AND `knows or ought reasonably to know both`
    AND `tradeable on a financial market in this jurisdiction`
    AND `knows or ought to know the recipient would likely deal or procure`
